Lobium - fingerprint config channel: browser reads the file, renderer reads the switch.

The sidecar writes lobium-fp.json and launches Lobium with --lobium-fp-config=<path>. The BROWSER
process reads that file once (cached; the same shape Chromium uses for GaiaConfig) and forwards its
base64 to every renderer as --lobium-fp-data, size-guarded, so the SANDBOXED renderer - which cannot
open the file itself - can parse it. Config forwarding reaches worker renderer processes too, so
lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current() is populated for dedicated, shared and service workers.

Every failure path LOG(ERROR)s: a present-but-unparseable config must never silently fall back to
the host fingerprint without a trace.

LOCAL EXPOSURE, accepted for now. The base64 payload sits on the renderer's argv, so anything on the
box that can read another process's command line - /proc/<pid>/cmdline on Linux, any process-listing
tool on Windows - can read the whole persona: geolocation coordinates, timezone, screen, GPU and
media-device counts. No page can reach argv, so this is not a detection surface; it is a privacy
leak to co-tenants and to local software that logs command lines. Closing it means a non-argv
transport (a shared-memory handle or a pipe inherited by the child), which is also what would remove
the 28 KiB size guard below - the two are the same piece of work.

This patch is ONLY the transport. The parser and all shared kernels live in the added module
//components/lobium_fp/ (staged by lobium/build.ps1 / build.sh, wired by core/build-gn.patch), and
each SURFACE that reads Current() is its own patch so an upstream change rejects in exactly one
place:
  * core/navigator-ua-ch.patch          navigator.* + User-Agent + Sec-CH-UA
  * fingerprint/canvas-farbling.patch   canvas 2D / OffscreenCanvas readback
  * fingerprint/webgl-surfaces.patch    WebGL vendor/renderer, caps, pixel farbling
  * fingerprint/audio-context.patch     Web Audio farbling
  * fingerprint/screen-dpr.patch        screen geometry / colour depth / DPR
  * ... see patches/series and hooks.md

Hook point: content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc.

